# Branching / Hotfix Playbook Guard

Canonical playbook: `docs/workflow/branching-hotfix-playbook.md`.

## When this applies

Before acting on (or recommending) any of: new long-lived branches, hotfixes for a tagged build, tagging/publishing while feature work is open, PATCH vs alpha bumps for bugfixes, or “fix prod only on main and ship later.”

## Model (allowed)

| Line | Role |
|------|------|
| **`main`** | Ongoing development / next MINOR once a release is being finalized elsewhere |
| **`releaseX.Y`** (e.g. `release2.7`) | Opened when the **official is near** and development must continue on `main`. Planned release is **moved** here: finalize (beta/rc/official), then bugfixes and PATCH / minor maintenance releases. Port fixes to `main` via PR |
| **Tags** | Immutable; for that MINOR after the split, cut from `releaseX.Y` |
| **Short-lived `hotfix/…`** | Only when even the ship line must not ship as-is |

## Warn the user (stop and ask) if they are about to

| Violation | Prefer instead |
|-----------|----------------|
| Create permanent `develop` or `alpha` | Use `main` + `releaseX.Y` when official is near; pre-release = version/tag on the ship line |
| Finalize / tag the planned MINOR from dirty `main` while `releaseX.Y` exists | Commit and tag on `releaseX.Y` |
| Merge next-MINOR features from `main` into `releaseX.Y` | Keep features on `main`; only cherry-pick fixes the release truly needs |
| Urgent patch for a **tagged** build by shipping unfinished ship-line commits | Short-lived `hotfix/…` from that **tag**, then port to `releaseX.Y` and PR to `main` |
| Leave a release-line fix **without** a PR/cherry-pick to `main` when `main` still has that path | Always port the code fix |
| Tag a commit where `version.py` ≠ tag (without `v`) | Bump/align `version.py` first (explicit approval) |
| Mid-alpha cycle: PATCH the **last official** for a community tester fix | Next `X.Y.Z-alpha.N+1` / `-beta.N+1` (after approval), unless patching prod `:latest` |
| Rewind a ship line’s `version.py` to an official PATCH while a newer pre-release continues | Port **code** only; leave `version.py` on the ongoing alpha/beta/rc |
| Rewrite / force-push a published tag | New tag with a new approved version string |

## Default (no warning needed)

- When official is near and development continues: open `releaseX.Y` from the freeze tag/commit; finalize and maintain there
- Bugfix / PATCH on `releaseX.Y` (or `main` if no release branch) → **D** (if needed) → **B** or **C**; PR fix to `main`
- Short-lived `hotfix/…` from tag only when users need a build **now** and the ship line must not ship yet

## How to remind

One short warning + point to the playbook path + ask which path they want. Do not silently create `develop`/`alpha`, skip PRs to `main`, or rewrite tags.
